cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AxonOS or its conformance suite in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "axonos-conformance: byte-exact conformance suite for the AxonOS Consent Protocol"
abstract: >-
  A byte-identical conformance surface for the AxonOS RFC-0005 capability manifest
  and RFC-0006 intent wire format. Canonical vectors are emitted from the shipping
  implementation and re-checked in CI across Rust, Python, C, JavaScript, and Java,
  with a C-ABI shared library and a hand-written x86-64 assembly encoder.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yermakou
    given-names: Denis
    email: "connect@axonos.org"
    affiliation: "The AxonOS Project"
    website: "https://axonos.org"
license: "Apache-2.0 OR MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AxonOS-org/axonos-conformance"
url: "https://axonos.org"
keywords:
  - brain-computer interface
  - conformance
  - wire format
  - ABI
  - no_std
  - Rust

# The version of the conformance suite.
#
# This file had none. A citation file exists to say which version somebody is
# citing, and this one named a title, an abstract, an author and a licence
# while leaving unanswered the question it was written to answer — so anyone
# citing it cited "the conformance suite", which cannot be checked later.
#
# It is also the only place this repository states a version: there is no
# manifest, because a suite of vectors is not a package. The radar's card
# generator reads it here, and reported this project as Planned until the field
# existed.
#
# Matches the v1.1.0 tag. Bumped when a vector changes or a language is added,
# not when prose is edited.
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-13"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AxonOS-org/axonos-conformance"
url: "https://axonos.org"
